abstract: >
  This repository contains the full materials of a PRISMA 2020 systematic review
  on Digital Twins for energy optimization and smart building management,
  covering publications from 2015 to 2025 across four databases (Scopus, Web of
  Science, IEEE Xplore, SpringerNature). 704 raw records were reduced to 45
  included studies through a multi-stage screening pipeline assisted by Large
  Language Models (Gemini 2.5 Flash, Claude Opus) under human supervision,
  with all decisions validated by the full 5-member team. The repository
  includes the final IEEE-formatted article, the complete Python pipeline,
  decision artefacts (CSVs), and a technical mapping of the 45 included studies
  identifying EnergyPlus, Python, and Model Predictive Control as the dominant
  stack — while flagging the complete absence of studies in tropical maritime,
  ultra-marine, and coastal climates as a critical research challenge.
